  "description": "ICOCUA crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 42/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C108 H112 Ce1 Mn8 N4 O36. From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn1G (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn1A (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn1F (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2G (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2A (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2F (Mn) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 16 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.026-3.335 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 80.64-121.71°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C108H112CeMn8N4O36.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
